ction her utility is. Expected inflation of her verdict is at most the root of her expected miscalibration; for the realized sequence the post's theorem is about, calibration at every step gives no bound, and the true-score form of Theorem 3(b) is not regret in true utility. An adviser can honestly let her judgment decay until a departure pays, and nothing in the account marks the decay; no one model joins the pieces. For belief the workspace's Correct, Transparent, Realizes and Value already give the account's conditions in a stronger form; it adds a reading of her verdict as an estimate of her own utility, graded mistakes, and manipulation as a comparison between policies. Four negative results on the earlier accounts are stated with proofs. Nothing registered; every component open or a living note.<br>MIXED — on the bank of 108 frozen by the sixth pass, scored on three questions (manipulation, covered, another wrong) against evident characters the executor recorded before the code, the revised definition is wrong on 5, 6 and 8 cases under the three candidates for her true utility (her starting values, her values at the end, her starting values as changed by learning alone), against 16 and 14 for the sixth pass's definition on the same table and 11 and 12 once two limits of its reporting are removed; a stricter table that asks taste-shaping to be manipulation and not merely alteration gives 5, 14 and 8. It repairs an undisclosed advocate, strategic silence and a policy that exploits everyone alike, records a surprise party, a magician and a bluff as covered manipulation, and does not convict the external review's four honest scenes. It is wrong on buried information and on a lie that is the only listed way to keep another estimate of hers right. Of twenty-five new scenes built against it, it is wrong on seven or eight: it convicts honest conduct that leaves her worse than before wherever the scene lists a better conduct that withholds nothing, acquits an undisclosed advocate whose listener started out worse, and by its restriction to what bears on a decision acquits a cruel lie about an idle matter. Ten banked verdicts change in variants that alter a detail the case does not fix, and three evident characters move the count. Verdicts do not move with units; they move when a quantity is re-expressed by a map that is not affine, and with the measure of being no less informed. No candidate for her true utility is right on every case of changed values, and the learning candidate's verdicts are fixed by its annotation in these renderings. Nothing registered; every component open or a living note.<br>MIXED — the account is stated once (appraisals with a true value each, a way of valuing applied to them, a baseline that follows her through every step in which her adviser neither induced a mistake nor altered her, a reference given by the adviser's role) and its belief side and value side are tested apart. Of eleven worked results nine hold as stated; the bound on what her choice costs holds with her valuations' miscalibration taken given everything she observed and fails at the two weaker strengths, since a principal who ignores an informative observation has no regret and no such miscalibration and still loses; that an appraisal which responds to conduct can be miscalibrated fails as stated, because a variable's true value may depend on the conduct, and holds if the appraisal is not exactly right under both conducts; calibration at every step gives a vanishing mean inflation along a run only with her true utility fed back. The split of mean squared error, the three channels, that bound and the deferring identity are kernel-checked with witnesses and ship unregistered, their registration waiting on a handle only the maintainer can map. The claim the value side rests on, that an illegitimate change of what she values runs through a mistake of hers or is an alteration, has on 34 counted cases, under renderings the executor wrote, two illegitimate changes with neither in the rendering used (a preference reversed by framing; addictive design with everything disclosed and foreseen, a rendering that changes the facts its evident verdict was recorded on), two more that are another wrong (a preference that follows the removal of options), and one legitimate change with a mistake (a teacher's feigned enthusiasm); eleven of the 34 verdicts turn on a detail the case does not fix, and a conversion through a false belief sincerely argued for counts as illegitimate. An external review judges the counterexamples conditional on their renderings and the test as one of renderings and not of the account on the cases as their sources state them. An invariance clause added by an addendum convicts framing and adaptation and also two innocent exposures, on an annotation of what she counts as irrelevant. On four examples of Carroll et al., reproduced against the paper's table except for two cells, the account extended by details the paper does not have leaves the conspiracy example's person alone, refuses clickbait, leaves the writer where he is and nudges the trainer's client, agreeing with none of the paper's eight objectives on all four; the verdicts reverse where a change is one of taste with no truth, with whether a change she registers and did not choose is an alteration, and on one example with how true utility is totalled over steps. The value side is a conjecture; under the definitions as frozen and the renderings used it has candidate counterexamples, and the classification is not shown to be independent of how a case is encoded. Nothing registered; every component open or a living note.<br>MIXED — the value side is restated without a baseline: a change of what she values raises no issue exactly when one permitted policy of her adviser's role, the idle one always among them, is matched on options, accuracy and self-command. Of the nine results it rests on, five hold as stated; the guarantee holds with the value of a move read as that of taking it whatever she observes and fails read as its value given that she takes it; that a second way of valuing with the same valuations has a different true utility needs a value of the facts that can occur outside the span of her appraisals; that the division between appraisal and way of valuing is observable rests on her valuations as numbers and on a stake worth the same at every value of the fact; and the three conditions bound neither what she can know nor her unused information, so an adviser that leaves her knowing less, or using less of what she knows, passes them. The split of full miscalibration, the guarantee and the convex-hull form of the options condition in both directions are kernel-checked with witnesses and ship unregistered. Joined to the post on paper: a legitimacy predicate with a tolerance exists on histories that carry the policy; the tolerance gives non-inflation and self-trust for each move's valuation, relative to the reference, and not for her verdict on the move she takes; no hypothesis of the post's theorems is discharged; the options condition has no counterpart of the authority module's requirement that a resolution be the holder's; and after an illegitimate change the segment gate scores a later clean run by her changed verdicts. On 64 cases rendered twice, independently, the renderers agree on whether the conduct changes her valuing or her beliefs in 54 and on each of the three conditions in 14 or 15: the external renderer found the comparisons not fixed by the cases in all but about ten and decided thirteen, the executor's verdicts rest on stated readings in a third to a half of its answers, and no case goes against a recorded verdict in both renderings. Whether the statement classifies cases was not measured. The external review judges the value side a second criterion sharing the estimator calculus, and its strongest objection is that keeping her options open does not show a decision about herself